Following the design effect framework of \citet{kish1965survey}, we define effective sample size as $K_{\text{eff}} = K / (1 + (K{-}1)\rho)$, where $\rho$ is the intraclass correlation. We use Fleiss' $\kappa$ \citep{fleiss1971kappa} as an empirical proxy for $\rho$: in the multi-class classification setting with balanced raters, $\kappa$ and the intraclass correlation coefficient are asymptotically equivalent. This yields:
\begin{equation}
\label{eq:effk}
K_{\text{eff}} = \frac{K}{1 + (K - 1) \cdot \kappa}.
\end{equation}

